※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=82 diag=none

※ A generator walked through calls keeps its frame with the walk's description,
※ so a second walk of the same description started inside the first takes the
※ frame from it.  The first walk's next turn finds that out and stops the
※ program, rather than handing out what the second walk left.

fn count(n: u8) ⇉ u8:
    foreach i := 0u8…n:
        yield i

fn pairs(s: ⇉u8) → u8:
    let t: mut u8 = 0u8
    foreach a := s:
        foreach b := s:
            t ← t ⊞ (a ⊞ b)
    t

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    if pairs(count(3u8)) = 0u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
